    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1002">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1118" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/8–244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Financial and
                        Monetary Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collado</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-08-18">August 18, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to telegram 1965 of August 17, 10 p.m., to Moscow regarding
                    negotiations with Stepanov regarding the 3(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)
                    agreement. I note that there has apparently been extensive consultation <pb
                        facs="1129" n="1119" xml:id="pg1119"/> with the Treasury Department
                    regarding the terms of interest and amortization which might be appropriate and
                    that certain concessions may have been or will probably be made both in
                    connection with rate of interest and the period of grace.</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that all of the original documents on this matter were
                    undertaken by a subcommittee of which I was chairman, I am rather surprised that
                        FMA<anchor n="14" xml:id="d1002-f1"/> has not participated at all on this
                    matter. In addition, I have certain doubts regarding the extension of some of
                    the concessions which Treasury is being urged to make in order to please the
                        Russians.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d1002-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1002-f1" n="14" xml:id="d1002-f1-content">
                <p>Division of Financial and Monetary Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1002-f2" n="15" xml:id="d1002-f2-content">
                <p>Notation by Mr. Acheson: “I have been conducting these negotiations myself.
                    DA.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
